/docs/easyweek/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md

# ===== PR-11.1 EasyWeek cutover: operational artefacts, never tracked =====
# `outputs/` holds run reports, canary logs and operator exports. It was only in
# .git/info/exclude, which is local to one clone — a second machine would have
# tracked it. The migration writes reports here by default, so the rule belongs
# in the repository.
outputs/

# The migration PREPARATION stage's state directory (plan §29). It holds the
# operator review, the decision store and the generated customer directory —
# names, phone numbers and e-mail addresses. Covered by `outputs/` at the
# default path, and named explicitly so that moving the default does not
# silently start tracking personal data.
outputs/easyweek_migration_prepare/
easyweek_migration_prepare/

# Customer exports and any spreadsheet dropped into the tree. These are PII by
# definition: EasyWeek customer exports, Altegio client lists, visit-counter
# import files.
*.csv
*.xls
*.xlsx
!docs/**/*.example.csv

# Real cutover manifests. The committed template is
# docs/easyweek/migration_manifest.example.json; anything else is an operator's
# working copy and may name production locations, staff and services.
migration_manifest*.json
!docs/easyweek/migration_manifest.example.json
